 but  Momo is still doubting himself saying  easier said than done he thinks it's  impossible the clouds refuse to come out  no matter how hard he tries he's  beginning to lose resolve as he says he  can't with tears in his eyes but then we  get the flashback of that day in the  Burning Castle 20 years ago we jump to  Toki telling her son Momo that he should  go with kinemon and the others she's  certain that Momo will be able to revive  the kozuki clan after he leaps 20 years  into the future now I love time travel  and think this is super cool but part of  me is like kaido will just get stronger  over the next 20 years but I guess what  son got Luffy in the picture it really  doesn't matter Momo is crying and  doesn't want to do it at first he wants  Toki and hiri to go with him but kinemon  tells him to think about his mom's  feelings he tells Momo that no man  should question the result of a woman  who speaks with such conviction and that  nothing could be more shameful and Momo  replies well he's not a man but a child  which is something that's easy for us to  forget and to lose patience with Momo  but we shouldn't the dude is a little  kid and we can't just expect an  eight-year-old to just man up all at  once kinemon continues to remind Momo of  his responsibility now though he says  with Odin that he's no longer just an  heir he wants Momo to give them a chance  to fight kinemon would rather Die With  Honor on the battlefield than wait and  burn to death in the castle he says he  will do anything to wield his sword for  his Lord momonosuke with kinemon bowing  down to him Momo continues to cry but  shows resolve through the tears and says  mother I will be on my way now powerful  stuff and we can imagine how hard this  is for Toki as well who wants to mother  her little boy but also knows what needs  to be done she says yes holding back her  own tears and we jump back to the  present Momo realizes he'll never be  able to face his mom again if he left  things like this with Newfound resolve  he keeps on trying to produce working  flame clouds even though it's not going  that well we jump back to the epic fight  and kaido says to Luffy you grabbed  lightning he laughs at how ridiculous it  is I said last time that he probably  grabbed it but it wasn't clear if he  produced it before or if he just grabbed  it from the sky so now we know he didn't  produce the lightning just grabbed it  from the sky and tunified it so  potentially he can't just produce any  element but we can't say that 100 for  sure he uses gomukomuno Thunderbolt and  throws the lightning like Zeus himself  but kaido just Dodges it which is a bit  anticlimactic after leaving us with that  final panel out last time I really wish  Oda would have let us see that attack  land but perhaps he's building up for a  satisfying attack to happen next chapter  as we'll get into in a bit either way  it's clear that kaido is not messing  around he's not arrogant enough to just  take hits like that anymore and knows he  must avoid them which is a good sign he  even says to Luffy that Luffy can keep  playing around but in the end a strong  devil fruit power isn't enough to  conquer the Seas while he says this he  hits Luffy setting him flying and Luffy  even uses another lightning bolt as a  kind of pull trampoline and bounces off  of it to get back to kaido but it's  interesting what kaido says I think Oda  is talking to the fans who think Luffy  is too overpowered now when it comes to  his double fruit I already said it's  fine because Luffy was always a kind of  chosen one and not everyone who got this  special fruit was good enough to awaken  it but here Oda is making it clear just  because he got to this point doesn't  mean that Conquering the Seas will be  easy kaido goes on to smash Luffy in the  face with his Club adding that Roger had  no fruit power and he still brought the  world to heal Shanks is probably a  similar example of someone who  accomplished a lot 